abstract: >
  AtmoSR is a dual-branch model for atmospheric spatial downscaling.
  It combines a fixed bicubic branch with a residual convolutional
  neural network and uses a Global Relative Error loss to normalize
  four supervised physics constraints.
keywords:
  - atmospheric downscaling
  - super-resolution
  - ERA5
  - physics constraints
  - Global Relative Error
  - PyTorch
